cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite the manuscript and this release."
title: "UOT_KR: Transport Representation and Conditional Decoding for Cross-Chain Forensic Fund-Flow Correspondence"
version: "1.0-vldb-submission"
abstract: >-
  Artifact release for the manuscript "Non-One-to-One Cross-Chain Forensic Fund Flow
  Correspondence: Transport Representation and Conditional Decoding". It contains the
  method implementation (risk-weighted unbalanced optimal transport over flow segments,
  directional conditional decoding, coverage-qualified abstention), the three released
  experiment lines (R5 post-hoc hyper-parameter sensitivity and cost-component ablation;
  R6 post-hoc direct-kernel k control; R7 degree-calibrated hash-locked one-shot
  confirmatory kernel ranking), the frozen confirmatory package with its independent
  validator, the figure/table authoring package with provenance audits, and a
  risk-field empirical audit released as a negative result.
type: software
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/3074669057/UOT_KR"
keywords:
  - cross-chain forensics
  - anti-money laundering
  - fund-flow correspondence
  - unbalanced optimal transport
  - Sinkhorn decoding
  - semi-synthetic evaluation
  - reproducibility
